# What a trimmed commit keeps of the upstream commit it is made from, and all of it has to be
# there: an upstream commit that lacks anything named here is refused, not trimmed without it.
#
# With every backend off, Dawn's root `CMakeLists.txt` adds `third_party`, `src/utils` and
# `src/tint` and no other directory, and the three gitlinks are what Tint builds from. A newer Dawn
# may read a file this list does not name; that shows when Tint is configured, and the answer is a
# line here and a commit made again.
#
#   tree     a directory, kept whole
#   file     one file
#   gitlink  one submodule entry, kept at the commit upstream pins

tree     src/cmake
tree     src/tint
tree     src/utils

file     .gitattributes
file     .gitignore
file     .gitmodules
file     AUTHORS
file     CMakeLists.txt
file     LICENSE
file     README.md
file     third_party/CMakeLists.txt

gitlink  third_party/abseil-cpp
gitlink  third_party/spirv-headers/src
gitlink  third_party/spirv-tools/src
